{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
  "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Maryland-National Capital Park and Planning Commission",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Thank you, Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: There are four important facts about the memorial at issue, the Peace Cross, that explain why it should not be dismembered or destroyed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Do you know how many other parks are like this one?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "American Legion",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CARVIN: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: While the Peace Cross should be upheld under any sensible Establishment Clause analysis, we submit the Court should analyze it under the Town of Greece coercion test, which prohibits tangible interference with religious liberty, as well as proselytizing, for a number of reasons."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice KAGAN: Well, is there?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice KAVANAUGH: Presumptively valid and can -- that presumption can be overcome when?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Carvin",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CARVIN: Your Honor, we could have a bright line test that only formal coercion is prohibited, but I don't think that would satisfy this Court because the dangers of the Establishment Clause posed by coercion, which is tangible threat to liberty, may -- could be reached indirectly through the sorts of things I'm talking about."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice GORSUCH: Why am I not proselytizing religion when I say \"In God we trust\" but I am when I say \"In Jesus Christ we trust\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "General Wall",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "GENERAL WALL: I think, Justice Alito, it makes it an easier case. But what I would say is we have four basic buckets of litigation over displays in the state and federal courts. You've got war memorials, Ten Commandments, holiday displays, and other forms of symbolic expression, like mottos or seals."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Monica L. Miller",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0002-0005",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this particular case that this cross was put up to commemorate the deaths of 49 real people and that this was done in the wake of World War I?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Monica L. Miller",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. MILLER: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court: I think we can all agree that the Establishment Clause at the very least prohibits the government from preferring one religion over another religion."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MONICA L. MILLER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Could I -- could I ask a question that picks up on a question that Justice Ginsburg asked earlier?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0002-0009",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Well, just to follow up on Justice Gorsuch's question, what if you had one letter from one person who purported to be offended by it? Would that be enough to support your argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I guess I am curious in response to Justice Kagan, you say we shouldn't apply Lemon in this case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Miller",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 70,
        "start": 70
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "On the contrary, Your Honor, I think that Lemon is very useful. I think when you -- you heard the arguments earlier today, they talked about context, they talked about purpose, they talked about effect. Those -- that's the crux of Lemon."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "so I'm clear. The distinction between the Ten Commandments and the cross?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Miller",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 78,
        "start": 78
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The 9/11 cross that Petitioners speak of is a perfect example. It sits in an exhibit panel along with other pieces of rubble and an explanatory plaque about how it came to be."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0004-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 87,
        "start": 87
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: I guess my question was, in thinking about our role, what is the role of this Court in a case like this?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0004-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "REBUTTAL ARGUMENT OF NEAL K. KATYAL ON BEHALF OF THE PETITIONER IN CASE NO. 18-18 MR. KATYAL: Thank you. Ours is a middle path between my three excellent friends. The easiest way to resolve this case in the -- is to say, in the wake of World War I, crosses like this one have an independent secular meaning."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Neal K. Katyal (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1717",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "51b20b1b42be1e401356a333af0691c6889fc081aa2d007d5c40afd3b4c729e8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-51b20b1b42be-0004-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 93,
        "start": 93
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KATYAL: Well, I think it would be very impossible for reasons that the -- for -- for reasons our brief explains to find it."
    },
    {
